/-!
# Concrete K1.2--K1.5 insertion point for Tag 73

This module exposes the exact interactive object consumed by the upstream
knowledge proof.  A successful checked deterministic refinement constructs
one `ConcreteFirstExecution`; every restoration is then the definitional map
`concreteRestoration execution generated`.  There is no restore-function
field, state-map premise, Fiat--Shamir cover, or compiler conclusion.

The probabilistic section names only the K1.2--K1.5 knowledge inequality on
the concrete interactive event.  It proves reusable expansion and normalized
arithmetic, but says nothing about how a Fiat--Shamir accepting sample enters
that event.  That latter inclusion belongs to the protocol-specific adaptive
lazy-oracle coupling.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace AspisK1.V7Tag73ConcreteKnowledgeInsertion

